      "summary": "Painted and carved wood speaker&#039;s staff [?]. From top to bottom the figures and forms are: a wedge shaped painted finial, perhaps representing a spear point, decorated with simple geometric designs, followed by a cylindrical [spear shaft?] section; over a head, with a cylindrical section underneath, joined to the potlatch rings of a hat, sitting on the head of a complete figure; below is a short cylindrical section, and a three dimensional copper form, the upper section on one side carved with a human head in high relief; followed by a cylindrical section joining into the hat rings of a second figure, which follows onto the head of a hawk [?], followed by a final cylindrical section.",
